1
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:32,640
Episode 1 How could this have happened?

2
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:35,540
I can't believe.

3
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,660
We totally fell for it.

4
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:59,360
Let's go.

5
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,960
Having managed to halt the
lover's invasive attack,

6
00:02:15,240 --> 00:02:19,337
Jotaro and company choose to avoid
the political unrest in Iran and Iraq,

7
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:25,240
and instead cross the Arabian Sea at Karachi
to arrive at the United Arab Emirates.

8
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,235
Now then, if you'd be so kind
as to sign this document,

9
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,656
everything will be squared away, sir.

10
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,070
Hmm.

11
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:34,480
Right here, yes?

12
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,240
Man, oh man.

13
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:43,257
You know, I'm the kind of guy who'd
do almost anything for a pretty girl,

14
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:44,340
even by a car.

15
00:02:44,520 --> 00:02:45,860
My, aren't you sweet.

16
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:49,627
How would you feel about the two
of us having dinner sometime?

17
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:51,717
Sorry, Polnareff.

18
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:56,400
I hate to interrupt when you're
obviously so busy, but... Mr. Joestar!

19
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,377
Come on, it's time to leave.

20
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:59,290
Seriously.

21
00:02:59,373 --> 00:03:01,077
Try not to mess with the hair.

22
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,278
Do you know how hard it is
to make it look this good?

23
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,740
as if anybody cares about your hairdo.

24
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:08,020
You're driving.

25
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:09,670
Radio.

26
00:03:10,180 --> 00:03:11,800
Au River, mademoiselle.

27
00:03:12,840 --> 00:03:14,300
Hey, Mr. Joestar,

28
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:17,057
I don't get why we're
riding in such a fancy,

29
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,434
expensive car in this sandy death trap.

30
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:23,485
Wouldn't it be better for us to
get an off-road vehicle instead?

31
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:29,700
Oh, there's a method to my madness.

32
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:34,140
C 'est magnifique!

33
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:35,873
This country's amazing!

34
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,259
Are you guys seeing what I am here?

35
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:41,557
It's like every house is a
crazy mansion or something.

36
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:42,470
Yeah.

37
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,200
In Tokyo, a house like one of these
would cost 3 or 4 billion yen.

38
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:51,806
However, for most people in this
country, it's standard living.

39
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:55,697
It wasn't but 20 years ago that
this place was a barren desert,

40
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:58,260
Though thanks to a thriving oil industry,

41
00:03:58,560 --> 00:04:01,031
it's grown into a playground for the rich.

42
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:04,337
The sun is merciless, but at
least with air conditioning,

43
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:06,857
it's perfectly comfortable inside the car.

44
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:08,620
So no complaints here.

45
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:10,810
Huh?

46
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,900
What's wrong, Kakyoin?

47
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:14,437
It's nothing.

48
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,057
I was just thinking about
how open it is here.

49
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:19,497
I know we could spot anyone following us,

50
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:23,992
but I just can't shake the feeling that
there's someone out there watching.

51
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:26,101
Yeah, can't say that I blame you.

52
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:28,600
Well, back to business.

53
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:31,797
I've given a bit of thought
to the route we should take.

54
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:35,640
About 100 kilometers northwest
is a village called Yarplein.

55
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:39,880
The desert and mountains make taking
a direct route near impossible.

56
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:42,800
It normally takes two
days to reach my car.

57
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,877
So to expedite the travel time, the
locals use a Cessna to get there.

58
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,377
If you want my opinion,

59
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:50,537
we should go to the
village and buy a Cessna

60
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:53,444
in order to cross the
vast Saudi Arabian desert.

61
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:57,417
You know, I've been apprehensive
about getting anywhere near a plane.

62
00:04:57,500 --> 00:05:00,037
If a stand user attacked
and the plane went down,

63
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:02,297
we'd be putting innocent
lives in harm's way.

64
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,757
But if we had a Cessna,
I could be the pilot.

65
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,497
We'd be able to save a
couple of days for sure.

66
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:11,057
Flying in a Cessna with a man
who's been in three plane crashes.

67
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,669
Yeah, that seems like
a perfect idea to me.

68
00:05:16,140 --> 00:05:18,140
That comment notwithstanding,

69
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:20,777
our priority should be
crossing the desert.

70
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:23,197
and hightailing it to
the village of Yarpline.

71
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,440
It'll take us one day on Camelback.

72
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,230
Camelback?

73
00:05:27,313 --> 00:05:29,453
A Cessna is one thing, but on Camelback?

74
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,736
I've never ridden a camel in my life!

75
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:35,267
Just leave everything to me.

76
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:38,537
I know these creatures well, and
I'll teach you how to ride them.

77
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:41,580
You boys sit back and
watch the magic happen.

78
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,280
You want camels, you say?

79
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:48,317
Sure I have them, but
they're gonna cost you,

80
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,753
my friend, and they need a gentle touch.

81
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:55,577
We're kind of in a life-or-death situation
here, so we need them, whatever it takes.

82
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,425
As for payment, how about
a trade for that car?

83
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:04,000
I couldn't possibly accept such a
generous offer! Yeah, Mr. Joestar!

84
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:07,184
And besides, you literally
just bought that car!

85
00:06:07,900 --> 00:06:11,557
What other reason did you think I had
to buy such a fancy, expensive car?

86
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:14,757
It's true an off-road vehicle
would perform better here,

87
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:16,605
but we're not in the big city.

88
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:19,191
We can't just write a check in this place.

89
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,600
And cash isn't accepted here.

90
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:25,995
In my experience, trading is far more
effective in places such as these.

91
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:29,592
If you try to buy safety for
cheap in a time of emergency,

92
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:32,565
you'll find yourself even
worse off in the end.

93
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:36,917
Besides, I don't know about you, but
I think we've suffered enough already.

94
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,380
Hey, mister! Huh?

95
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,160
I take it this seals the deal?

96
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,180
Oh, hey, you know what?

97
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:47,753
To make things a little more even, I'd
like the water in those tanks, too.

98
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:50,837
It's the most important thing
when you're in the desert.

99
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:54,460
But the water isn't nearly
as valuable as your car, sir.

100
00:06:54,760 --> 00:06:57,600
You are very strange indeed, sir.

101
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,116
All right, everyone.

102
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,849
Let's get ready, shall we?

103
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:04,460
Crossing the desert will be no easy task.

104
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:05,974
Brace yourselves, men.

105
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:12,500
Man, that stinks!

106
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,260
Hey, Mr.

107
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,137
Joestar, how the heck are we supposed
to get on one of these things?

108
00:07:17,220 --> 00:07:18,867
It's like three meters tall!

109
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,917
Allow me to demonstrate the
proper way to mount a camel.

110
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:25,059
You have to make them sit
first and then you get on.

111
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,940
Like I said, make them
sit and then get on.

112
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,937
You see, just like this.

113
00:07:34,020 --> 00:07:36,900
You make them sit, and
then you get on them.

114
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:39,700
Give me a minute.

115
00:07:39,900 --> 00:07:43,420
Any second this beast is gonna
sit, then let me saddle up.

116
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:47,360
Hey, sit down, would you?

117
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,140
Damn it, you star! Mr.

118
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:52,077
Joe Star, you have ridden one
of these before, haven't you?

119
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:54,097
I will have you know that
I've watched Lawrence

120
00:07:54,180 --> 00:07:56,980
of Arabia three times
now from start to finish.

121
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:59,960
I know all too well how to ride a camel,

122
00:08:00,220 --> 00:08:02,577
although two of those times
I slept through half of it.

123
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,557
You learned to ride from a movie?

124
00:08:04,640 --> 00:08:08,580
So you're saying you've never
actually ridden one before?

125
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:19,320
The saliva makes great
sunscreen, the more you know.

126
00:08:21,580 --> 00:08:22,580
Listen up.

127
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:24,517
When you're handling an animal,

128
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:28,247
it's absolutely imperative to
understand exactly how it feels.

129
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,420
And I mean exactly.

130
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:34,531
Here, doesn't this yummy apple
look absolutely scrumptious?

131
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,760
It's really good.

132
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:37,110
Come on.

133
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,620
Come on.

134
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:40,140
There's a good boy.

135
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,080
You see?

136
00:08:42,300 --> 00:08:43,880
I made the camel sit down.

137
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:48,924
If you just take the time to get inside
its head, it'll sit down for you for sure.

138
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,340
Whoa, I did it!

139
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:57,540
Whoa, it's so high off the ground.

140
00:08:57,980 --> 00:09:00,237
By the way, did you know camels?

141
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:04,537
Can close their nostrils to keep
the sand out and before I forget,

142
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:07,337
you're forbidden from
making Stupid camel jokes!

143
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:08,317
Is that understood?

144
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:11,017
Your turn now, you greenhorns!

145
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:13,557
Get to learn the finer
points Of riding a camel!

146
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:15,117
Listen up!

147
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:19,157
The first thing you need to know is that
camels don't walk anything Like horses!

148
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,237
The front and back legs on either
side move forward together,

149
00:09:22,320 --> 00:09:25,257
so these things can sway a Lot
but don't let that throw you off!

150
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:29,117
If you find a way to ride with a camel's
rhythm, I know you'll Be just fine!

151
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,157
For example!

152
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:32,357
Yeah! Hey! Wait!

153
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,737
You're going too fast!

154
00:09:33,820 --> 00:09:34,737
Slow down!

155
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:37,337
Listen to me! Damn it! Yeah!

156
00:09:37,420 --> 00:09:39,600
I didn't tell you to go that way!

157
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:44,610
Okay!

158
00:09:44,693 --> 00:09:48,909
Then now that everyone's gotten the hang
of mounting and riding their camels!

159
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:51,830
All right!

160
00:09:51,913 --> 00:09:53,457
We have a desert to get through!

161
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:55,397
The time has arrived! Men!

162
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,127
Onward toward the northwest!

163
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,877
Hey, now, wait just a minute!

164
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,790
Hey!

165
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:12,997
Something's wrong.

166
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,910
Huh?

167
00:10:13,993 --> 00:10:15,417
I still haven't been able to shake the

168
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:17,997
feeling that someone out
there is watching us.

169
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:18,910
Hmm?

170
00:10:22,680 --> 00:10:26,327
Kakyoin, don't you think you
might be worrying a bit too much?

171
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,947
I mean the palm leaves
will erase our tracks.

172
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:32,937
Plus, we can see for
kilometers in all directions.

173
00:10:33,020 --> 00:10:34,902
If someone were here, we'd know.

174
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,474
Actually, I think he's on to something.

175
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,840
I feel some sort of presence, too.

176
00:10:41,060 --> 00:10:43,531
Hey, Jotaro, why don't you go take a look?

177
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,357
How about it?

178
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,852
Do you see anything suspicious out there?

179
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,577
No, nothing.

180
00:11:01,660 --> 00:11:02,778
Nothing whatsoever.

181
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:05,980
Even so, something's not right here.

182
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,242
But what is it?

183
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:11,080
Hey, let's hurry up and go.

184
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:13,190
Yeah.

185
00:11:13,273 --> 00:11:14,780
Let's get as far away as we can.

186
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,157
We'll keep pressing forward until
the sun goes down this evening,

187
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,960
then stop to pitch our tents.

188
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:23,057
It's much too dangerous
for us to travel at night.

189
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:26,140
I only wish we could get
out of this freaking heat.

190
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:27,439
Just look at this.

191
00:11:27,580 --> 00:11:29,462
It's reading 50 degrees Celsius.

192
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,860
Yeah, it is hot out here.

193
00:11:32,240 --> 00:11:35,946
But then again, the weather is
at its hottest right around now.

194
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:38,520
Eight o 'clock? What?

195
00:11:39,460 --> 00:11:40,940
Jotaro, check your watch.

196
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,494
What time does it say?

197
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:45,740
It's ten past eight.

198
00:11:47,080 --> 00:11:48,180
Hey, old man!

199
00:11:48,400 --> 00:11:49,660
My watch is correct.

200
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:52,660
We lost track of time, but...

201
00:11:53,140 --> 00:11:54,611
What the hell's going on?

202
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,240
According to my watch, it's past 8 p .m.

203
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:01,060
So why isn't the sun setting?

204
00:12:02,520 --> 00:12:03,780
This is impossible.

205
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,042
The thermometer is jumping
to 60 degrees Celsius.

206
00:12:14,060 --> 00:12:16,400
No, the sun isn't setting at all.

207
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:17,497
It's actually...

208
00:12:17,580 --> 00:12:20,080
It's actually rising higher in the west!

209
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:22,968
Wait, could it be that
that sun is really...

210
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:24,060
A stand?

211
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:36,857
I don't understand how such
a thing is even possible!

212
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:39,234
How could this sun actually be a stand?

213
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,034
Quickly, take cover behind those rocks!

214
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,920
How the hell could that sun be a stand?

215
00:12:46,700 --> 00:12:47,880
We're such fools!

216
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,057
How did we miss this?

217
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,877
I knew that we were being watched,

218
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:53,737
but I never thought this is
why I couldn't see our stalker.

219
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:56,157
At this rate, that sauna's
gonna burn all day.

220
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,380
No, all night long.

221
00:12:57,760 --> 00:12:59,000
Oh, nom de dieu!

222
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:01,677
It's going to roast us like a
bunch of rotisserie chickens!

223
00:13:01,760 --> 00:13:03,054
We're totally screwed!

224
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:04,810
Yeah.

225
00:13:04,893 --> 00:13:06,518
Though I doubt it'll take that long.

226
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:11,137
The thing is, a sauna can dangerously
raise the body's temperature in minutes.

227
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,985
Okay, then how do we fight it?

228
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:15,315
C 'est des conneries!

229
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,397
It's 70 degrees Celsius!

230
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:21,080
And to add insult to injury, we can't
tell if the stand is close or not.

231
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:23,438
The distance is impossible to judge.

232
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:28,080
Our only option here is to
quickly take out the stand user.

233
00:13:29,180 --> 00:13:30,520
Indeed, the user.

234
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,157
He has to be nearby.

235
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:33,560
We have to find him.

236
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,035
He must have a way to conceal himself.

237
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,957
And somehow he's been
following us all this time.

238
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:39,977
Hang on a minute.

239
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:43,097
What if it's like the lovers
we encountered in Pakistan?

240
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:45,697
Maybe this guy has a stand
he can use from far away.

241
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,940
Hey, that's not the case this time.

242
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:51,457
Sure, a weak STAN can be
controlled from a distance,

243
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:53,422
but this sun is just too strong.

244
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:56,017
The energy it's emitting is incredible.

245
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,240
The STAN user has to be nearby.

246
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,237
Hey, check it out.

247
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,357
The camels are starting to
collapse from exposure to the heat,

248
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:18,020
and this wading isn't getting us anywhere.

249
00:14:18,340 --> 00:14:21,537
I'll use Hierophant to do some
reconnaissance around the area.

250
00:14:21,620 --> 00:14:25,091
Kakyoin, I'm only searching
for the stand's rough location.

251
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:30,142
Once we know how far away it actually is,
we might just be able to locate the user.

252
00:14:31,820 --> 00:14:36,680
20 meters, 40 meters, 60
